-- title:
--   Smooth proper curve model covering the k-points of Spec A
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field and let $y \colon Y \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ be a morphism of schemes that is separated and locally of finite type. Let $A$ be a commutative ring that is an integral domain, equipped with a $k$-algebra structure making it of finite type over $k$, and assume $\operatorname{ringKrullDim} A = 1$. Let $\varphi \colon \operatorname{Spec} A \to Y$ be a morphism such that $\varphi$ followed by $y$ equals the morphism $\operatorname{Spec} A \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ induced by the structure map $k \to A$, i.e. $\varphi$ is a morphism over $k$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a scheme $C$, a morphism $c \colon C \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ that is proper and smooth of relative dimension $1$, with $C$ integral, together with an open subscheme $U \subseteq C$ and a morphism $\psi \colon U \to Y$ such that $\psi$ followed by $y$ equals the inclusion $U \hookrightarrow C$ followed by $c$ (so $\psi$ is a $k$-morphism), and such that for every section $a \colon \operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ of the structure morphism of $A$ over $k$ there is a morphism $p \colon \operatorname{Spec} k \to U$ which is a section of $U \hookrightarrow C$ followed by $c$ and satisfies $p$ followed by $\psi$ equals $a$ followed by $\varphi$; that is, every $k$-point of $\operatorname{Spec} A$ has its image in $Y$ realised as the image of a $k$-point of $U$.
--
--   This is the passage from an affine integral curve over an algebraically closed field to a smooth proper model: $C$ plays the role of the smooth complete curve with function field $\operatorname{Frac} A$, $U$ the locus where the induced rational map to $Y$ is defined, and the final clause records that all $k$-points of $\operatorname{Spec} A$ are accounted for by $k$-points of $U$. It feeds the valuative criterion used in [`AlgebraicGeometry.mem_of_isSeparated_of_forall_smoothProperCurve_opens_mem`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.mem_of_isSeparated_of_forall_smoothProperCurve_opens_mem), and its proof invokes the existence of a curve model over a perfect field together with a finiteness statement for fields generated by the image of a ring homomorphism.
